{%- comment -%}
  Single source of truth for which collection handles are Cultivators Club
  territory. Club pages get their own header, palette, fonts and access gate,
  and Club products are kept off every non-Club surface — all of which key off
  this list.

  Adding a Club collection used to mean editing six separate hardcoded checks
  (layout/theme.liquid twice, snippets/product-card.liquid,
  templates/collection.liquid, templates/product.liquid,
  templates/list-collections.liquid). Miss one and the new collection renders
  with the orange WRC header instead of the Club's. Add the handle here
  instead.

  Usage — the render tag has an isolated input scope, but its OUTPUT can be
  captured, which is what makes this work even inside the layout. Written
  below without tag delimiters, since Liquid still tokenises block tags
  inside a comment and a bare `if` here would read as unclosed:

    capture club_handles / render 'club-handles' / endcapture
    assign club_list = club_handles | strip | split: ','
    if club_list contains collection.handle   → it's a Club page

  Note the hub itself is matched separately with `contains 'cultivator'`,
  which also catches any future cultivator-* handle.
{%- endcomment -%}
the-cultivators-club,the-uniform,the-drops,club-accessories,core,collabs
